      "content": "5.1 Forest Cover"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "According to the India State of Forest Report 2021, Rajasthan has a total forest cover of approximately 16,655 sq km (4.87% of its geographical area), which is low compared to the national average of ~21.7%. Despite this, Rajasthan has rich biodiversity, particularly in the southern and eastern regions.",
      "id": "s2y2lm2"
    },
    {
